From: dinadur <59811564+dinadur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:31:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/18] B70: log-only Guardian groundedness check for
 quality-first product answers

Quality-first answers cite plain Markdown links, so the exact-quote groundedness
gate never runs for them. With HERMES_PRODUCT_GROUNDEDNESS_SHADOW=1, each linked
sentence is judged on a daemon thread against the best-matching 800-char windows
of the frozen extracted pages, and verdicts (p_yes, kind, excerpts, latency) are
appended to $HERMES_HOME/logs/groundedness-shadow.jsonl. The delivered answer,
its timing and the agent state are never changed; any failure is logged and
swallowed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
